  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In the expansion of \\((a+b)^n\\) there are \\(n+1\\) dissimilar terms. The number of dissimilar terms in the expansion of \\((a+b+c)^{10}\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(33\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(55\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(66\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(132\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "66"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p49.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each distinct term is \\(a^ib^jc^k\\) for nonnegative integers satisfying \\[ i+j+k=10. \\] By stars and bars, the number of such triples is \\[ \\binom{10+3-1}{3-1}=\\binom{12}{2}=66. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "A term is determined by nonnegative exponents \\(i,j,k\\) whose sum is \\(10\\)",
        "Count the solutions of \\(i+j+k=10\\) by stars and bars"
      ],
